UPDATE public.chapters SET content = regexp_replace(content, 'Soon\. Maybe today\. Maybe in the next day\. It is pregnant-adjacent, not pregnant itself — the <em>thélia</em> bond with pregnant women is not a bond the <em>thélia</em> survives outside their own range\. The creature is not going to die if it crosses further into this country\. But it is going to start being unable to follow us, and it is going to know when the point comes, and it is going to turn back\. I do not want to be sad when the turning comes\. I want to be — I want to prepare for it now, in the dark, so that I have the saying-goodbye already done in my head when the moment arrives\.', 'Soon. Maybe today. Maybe in the next day. The <em>thélia</em> do not cross into this country. Their range ends at the Hjord boundary. The creature has been stretching the range for me out of whatever instinct is driving it, and the range is not going to stretch much further. It is going to know when the point comes, and it is going to turn back. I do not want to be sad when the turning comes. I want to prepare for it now, in the dark, so that I have the saying-goodbye already done in my head when the moment arrives.'), updated_at = now() WHERE chapter_number = 54;